2026-10-23T18:41:25.7106262Z    image gate: coleman_ames_house_1811_prairie inland_architect_plate: verdict "differs", 2 difference(s) open: the porch's south return: beside the arch, from about x 467 to 507 px, the plate opens the entrance block's south return as a small arcade of round-arched lights on colonnettes with carved capitals, lighting the porch from the side; the build closes it in coursed stone (T-2991); the arcade's capitals (y 680-690 px) and crowns (y 647-660) step down across x 476-501, so it stands on a face receding from the front, about v 9.4-9.5 by the camera, short of the solved south corner at v 10.40; T-3005's re-read: the corner is ROUNDED, about 0.9 m radius, its front tangent at x 467-470 (v about 9.5) and its far side at about x 515-520 (the solve's x 510 is that edge), the downpipe's shoe at about y 816 px on the south face just behind it; the colonnettes step down because they run round the curve (on a 0.9 m radius, x 476, 490 and 501 px stand at about 8, 27 and 44 degrees from the front), not along a flat return. K01 has no rounded corner (T-3006); the arcade then stands on it (T-2991); T-3006 has built the round (0.9 m from grade, coursed on the front's beds), so the arcade now has its curve to stand on (T-2991, after the oriel's T-3007); the north pinnacle's shaft and cap: the plate's shaft stops at a band about y 342 px with a scaled pyramid over it to about y 320, under the block; K01 carries an engaged shaft past the face's eave (to 11.10 m), so the build's cap and plain pyramid stand about 20 px higher (y 317-325) and the pyramid is not scaled (T-3064)
