2026-10-23T18:41:25.7133690Z    image gate: henderson_house_1816_prairie chicagology_photo: verdict "differs", 11 difference(s) open: the porch and the front's canted bay stand about 1 m further south in the print than on the 1911 trace (the porch's columns read 60-75 px right of the print's through this camera): an alteration between the photograph and 1911, or the trace's or the camera's error, is T-2964's to argue; the raised mansard crown over the front's south end, with its own curb and iron cresting, standing higher than the main roof; the south flank's bay carried up through the cornice under its own mansard with a dormer in each face, and its cresting; built stopping under the cornice with a low hip; iron cresting along every roof deck; the dormers pedimented with carved cheeks; built round-headed; the window hoods carved, with a scrolled crest over each; built as K09's plain cornice-hood lintels; the porch columns' carved capitals and the balcony's pierced iron panels; built square capital blocks and square iron balusters, the railing 0.6 m where the print's reads nearer 1 m; the window over the door opens onto the balcony; built as a window; the fence's scrolled cast-iron panels and its tall posts; built as the kit's spears; the brick's tone: dark in the print; built in K01's buff brick (the print is monochrome, so the colour itself is not shown); the tall chimney stack behind the front's south end; placed on the south wall, its height and place not read
2026-10-23T18:41:25.7144827Z    image gate: house_1616_prairie landowner_1874_from_northeast: verdict "differs", 1 difference(s) open: the house: the build's front shows from x 961 px (its south wall) to the frame's edge, where the plate draws a tree's branches against the sky and, further off, the frame building beyond 1620's yard. The plate is of May 1874 and the record is of 1904, when the 1911 sheet's '2½B' brick house stands here; whether that house postdates the boards or the engraver left it out the plate cannot say, so the house is not taken down to the plate. A picture of 1616 after 1874 settles it
