2026-10-23T18:41:25.7249154Z    image gate: wheeler_house_1812_prairie c1955_front: verdict "differs", 9 difference(s) open: South stack: the photograph's shaft (x 21-39 px, cut by the print's edge) stands about 30 px south of the render's (x 53-77), the stack carried on the south wall's outer face in the gap to 1816, 0.3-0.9 m further out than K01's on_cornice stack can stand; and its top reads about 17 px higher, the camera's distance error off the front's plane (L-k01-1812-wheeler-stacks-3034); South wall: carried up past the mansard's curb to a coped top (y 166-170 px at the print's edge) with the stack on it, the slate face behind the gable's south shoulder rising to meet it, as T-3033 read in Levy's print; built as the mansard's south face, the parapet a kit change K01 does not make; South wall: its face in the gap to 1816 (x 22-75 px) reads a paler brick than the front, and carries a downpipe close to the front (x 66-71 px, about u 14.5), where the build's south-wall pipe stands about 1.5 m further back (x 43); the pipe may be later; Gable: the head is narrower and stands about 9 px (0.2 m) north of the build's: the south shoulder stone at x 205-225 px against the render's 182-232, the north at 335-352 against 315-350, the grid window centred at x 283 against 274; Levy's print reads the south side wider than the north and the build takes the mean (T-2951), so the two pictures disagree on the head's south half; Gable: the finial a tall urn on a moulded base, from about y 50 px to the head at y 100 (about 1.2 m), where the build's stops on a small square plinth at about y 85; Gable: the grid window in quoined side stones under a moulded hood, the shoulder stones' sunk panels and the kneelers' carved scrolls, as Levy's record already holds open; Third storey: the large window's middle light wider than the two beside it and the voussoirs alternating long and short into the brick, as Levy's record already holds open; Balcony: a solid carved stone panel in the middle of its front run with iron scrolls each side (x 230-335 px), as Levy's record already holds open; built as iron rail; South projection: the second storey's jambs rise past the window's head to carved caps under the cornice, and the paired window's mullion and hood are heavy dressed stone; built as K09's plain quoined surround stopping at the head
