2026-10-23T18:59:43.9432518Z       gate: T-0722. Both published paths carried the changelog verbatim until 2026-09-05, so the site shipped the same 1.31 MB twice — 4.1 % of its 32 MB budget on a byte-for-byte copy, growing at double the rate of the record, which is what put dev at 31.999 MB with no room for any PR to add a changelog entry. The shipped form is gated three ways: tools/validate.py refuses any two published files over 64 KB with identical bytes (so the duplicate cannot return the way it arrived); tools/test_changelog_mirror.mjs asserts the shim is what lands here and that it names the file it re-exports; and the smoke's What's-new leg loads the tab out of the published tree, which is the shim resolving or not.
